 prime.\n\n- $Q(x):$ $3\\,|\\,x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $P(x)⇒Q(x)≡¬P(x)∨Q(x),$ the corresponding truth sets can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={T}_{¬P∨Q} \\\\  & ={T}_{¬P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}={2,3,5,7}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the complement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{―}{T}}_{P} & =\\overset{―}{{2,3,5,7}} \\\\  & ={4,6,8,9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{Q}={3,6,9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={4,6,8,9}\\cup {3,6,9} \\\\  & ={3,4,6,8,9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381651 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198259 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "264cfe66-691e-550e-97ad-b71924332f21" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of an Implication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acec3bb4-18f5-52b2-bd10-2e97c6e66f4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381653} {:answer/id #uuid "6b356d5e-89a6-56cb-af93-b34e7bcb91bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381654} {:answer/id #uuid "36e2e920-ad1f-5dca-99c8-5b7e43aa12f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381655} {:answer/id #uuid "f2705ad3-87ba-5dc9-bf5c-ff4bd308cc08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381656} {:answer/id #uuid "d8c1056c-0a4c-555c-a419-380a9e72fa98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2705ad3-87ba-5dc9-bf5c-ff4bd308cc08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381656} :answer-field/id #uuid "aed36890-e9bf-5d40-865e-857f7e10ce2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381652}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2a8ee90e-4a33-5375-94bd-bb4f24a246fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-183318" :question/problem "Find the truth set of $P(x)⇒Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $R:$ \n\n- $P(x):$ $3x-1<5$\n\n- $Q(x):$ ${x}^{2}<4$" :question/worked-solution "Since $P(x)⇒Q(x)≡¬P(x)∨Q(x),$ the corresponding truth sets can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={T}_{¬P∨Q} \\\\  & ={T}_{¬P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- To find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-1 & <5 \\\\ 3x & <6 \\\\ x & <2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is\n${T}_{P}=(-\\infty ,2).$\nAs a result, the complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}=[2,\\infty ).$\n\n- To find the the truth set of $Q(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & <4 \\\\ -2 & <x<2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n${T}_{Q}=(-2,2).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & =[2,\\infty )\\cup (-2,2) \\\\  & =(-2,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415189 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198259 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "264cfe66-691e-550e-97ad-b71924332f21" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of an Implication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "387aad0d-bb8f-5b82-9e3e-546a38a316a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415167} {:answer/id #uuid "593a82e8-9e86-54b3-98d9-66e1b119d3aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415171} {:answer/id #uuid "9ef73a8c-ede8-54cc-8ecc-ab3bcf027fd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415174} {:answer/id #uuid "acc753ba-6cdc-5e6f-a65f-cf4670d35ffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415175} {:answer/id #uuid "f6a5945c-de3e-54a9-85e3-ea79b0853ec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "387aad0d-bb8f-5b82-9e3e-546a38a316a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415167} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0c1a066-5f9e-50ca-b88c-ecae2c88919a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415186}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f02a6ca7-3a4a-592a-bdf2-d7236cdc3430" :question/math-academy-id "q-183319" :question/problem "Find the truth set of $P(x)⇒Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $R:$ \n\n- $P(x):$ ${x}^{2}\\le 9$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $5x-3>7$" :question/worked-solution "Since $P(x)⇒Q(x)≡¬P(x)∨Q(x),$ the corresponding truth sets can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={T}_{¬P∨Q} \\\\  & ={T}_{¬P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- To find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\le 9 \\\\ -3 & \\le x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is \n${T}_{P}=[-3,3].$ \nAs a result, the complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}=(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (3,\\infty ).$\n\n- To find the the truth set of $Q(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-3 & >7 \\\\ 5x & >10 \\\\ x & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $Q(x)$ is\n${T}_{Q}=(2,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & =((-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (3,\\infty ))\\cup (2,\\infty ) \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (2,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381658 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198259 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "264cfe66-691e-550e-97ad-b71924332f21" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of an Implication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "377c3af9-ecc1-56c5-ae44-a1bc3a18929f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381660} {:answer/id #uuid "426bd88f-de02-5c87-b0d6-bd0e840ed766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381661} {:answer/id #uuid "2a944a8f-bcab-5d10-9b67-abface7825fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381662} {:answer/id #uuid "651f86c8-f6f2-5959-a1fd-5820cd2f474c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381663} {:answer/id #uuid "0c6d1942-660f-5e5c-95c0-636ca787a3a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "426bd88f-de02-5c87-b0d6-bd0e840ed766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381661} :answer-field/id #uuid "114d1f2d-d4d8-5039-bbd5-1bba2e0a02d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d732a9d-5a12-5283-982c-3d457f9987a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-183320" :question/problem "Find the truth set of $P(x)⇒Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $R:$ \n\n- $P(x):$ $4x-7\\ge 9$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $0<x<5$" :question/worked-solution "Since $P(x)⇒Q(x)≡¬P(x)∨Q(x),$ the corresponding truth sets can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={T}_{¬P∨Q} \\\\  & ={T}_{¬P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- To find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-7 & \\ge 9 \\\\ 4x & \\ge 16 \\\\ x & \\ge 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is\n${T}_{P}=[4,\\infty ).$\nAs a result, the complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}=(-\\infty ,4).$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n${T}_{Q}=(0,5).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,4)\\cup (0,5) \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,5).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415188 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198261 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6db336-845a-506a-b020-cced1b38e23a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Implications and Equivalences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f7f518c-488c-5d96-b7a5-43db3205b127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is not a multiple of $10,$ or $x$ is not a multiple of $5.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415163} {:answer/id #uuid "2a18ce88-661b-56f1-ab50-d4c0c0d859f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is a multiple of $10,$ and $x$ is a multiple of $5.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415165} {:answer/id #uuid "2d2d1990-533d-5e81-9481-787518e95fc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is a multiple of $10,$ or $x$ is a multiple of $5.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415166} {:answer/id #uuid "3b95cf79-290b-5ce6-acbf-d836c52800ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is not a multiple of $10,$ and $x$ is a multiple of $5.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415168} {:answer/id #uuid "f76ee12c-807a-54bc-af4b-5d50d1a1d4ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is not a multiple of $10,$ or $x$ is a multiple of $5.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f76ee12c-807a-54bc-af4b-5d50d1a1d4ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is not a multiple of $10,$ or $x$ is a multiple of $5.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415181} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bd67cf2-d2ad-524e-abec-5dd4e6b10fcb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "54b12d24-977a-54a5-aff6-9e8057c5e326" :question/math-academy-id "q-183351" :question/problem "$\\,$ If $x$ is a multiple of $10,$ then $x$ is a multiple of $5.$\n\nWhich of the following is logically equivalent to the conditional predicate above?" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote by $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $10.$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $5.$\n\nThen, our initial sentence can be written as $P(x)⇒Q(x),$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬P(x)∨Q(x).\n$$\n\nThe negation of $P(x)$ can be written as\n\n- $¬P(x):$ $x$ is not is a multiple of $10.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is not a multiple of $10,$ or $x$ is a multiple of $5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390177 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198260 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c5f2a86-209a-5bb3-a3f2-77d679adb0a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of an Equivalence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "841113e5-c450-59ac-8bc7-428da812b97a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390179} {:answer/id #uuid "363dbef4-2cb5-55b3-ada6-9f3bcd340c9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390180} {:answer/id #uuid "741cd058-59eb-5e0f-860b-99e896389c5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,0]\\cup [4,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390181} {:answer/id #uuid "97dd7bff-d511-560f-b23f-ffe623aab9ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,0]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390182} {:answer/id #uuid "843cf661-79b7-5be7-99ac-5624b829abad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[4,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "741cd058-59eb-5e0f-860b-99e896389c5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,0]\\cup [4,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390181} :answer-field/id #uuid "615dbf68-338e-5fff-88cf-1c09aa58eeb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea7c3e28-1d56-569a-9351-524a75784e57" :question/math-academy-id "q-183379" :question/problem "Find the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $R:$\n\n- $P(x):$ $4x-7\\ge 9$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $0<x<5$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have that\n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\n \n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇔Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- To find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-7 & \\ge 9 \\\\ 4x & \\ge 16 \\\\ x & \\ge 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is\n${T}_{P}=[4,\\infty ).$\nAs a result, the complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}=(-\\infty ,4).$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n${T}_{Q}=(0,5)$ \nand its complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}=(-\\infty ,0]\\cup [5,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q} & =[4,\\infty )\\cap (0,5) \\\\  & =[4,5) \\\\ {\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q} & =(-\\infty ,4)\\cap ((-\\infty ,0]\\cup [5,\\infty )) \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,0] \\\\ {T}_{P⇔Q} & =({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}) \\\\  & =[4,5)\\cup (-\\infty ,0] \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,0]\\cup [4,5).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198260 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c5f2a86-209a-5bb3-a3f2-77d679adb0a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of an Equivalence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d753a55c-d8d0-5731-a1a8-f9ffa2445839" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fd/fd9de70b000b0e00e8a799ad8f0814cdc95ea35aa3e5e32f85a94ceabc6dd074.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390186} {:answer/id #uuid "72b8ea46-0e7e-5df5-a15e-b6a3c6ac05ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ca/cabd391f691b5017dff012e9b777f82f0a1f9ce0b4c4afd0ba69bf426a00d90e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390187} {:answer/id #uuid "f7ea8b0a-b2c5-5604-a428-f7cfe010e169" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/16/16350cd516d6707e6e4fbba819a97d97f8594590fe91a68e8024785cb52edfd5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390188} {:answer/id #uuid "97a12ce2-ec25-58ab-a8f4-d779170d2481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4a/4a76d61d342fcf1503f00970b29da3d30c309f9f47b2276f3fe4d80a777cb85d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390189} {:answer/id #uuid "be266f09-d528-52fe-8dd4-049ebe7981eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/78/787284a02a119aa2a2135623ad6e50ad6e82295917866d0f137ed26a14a160aa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d753a55c-d8d0-5731-a1a8-f9ffa2445839" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fd/fd9de70b000b0e00e8a799ad8f0814cdc95ea35aa3e5e32f85a94ceabc6dd074.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390186} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c6163c2-3719-5918-b769-981cb8ff76dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "413ce96a-5ec8-5c19-a317-8e0248cda7da" :question/math-academy-id "q-183380" :question/problem "![](images/20/20783ac512f10184d50d2069792fdf42e701667125b07179236a8b0524b684b2.png)\n\nThe shaded regions above represent the truth sets of predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ defined over the universal set ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following is the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have that \n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\n \n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n![](images/01/0188e215f62afde3fa730642703fb6e2b213f8864f912ac0688d35fa29bb4db2.png)\n\nThen, we sketch the set ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}$ and ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}:$\n\n![](images/f4/f4df9eb071e2deb4c79c8928a7b9e60f3341bba827a5fbb328e864d2de9a5803.png)\n\nAs a result, ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}$ is the following: \n\n![](images/f1/f17a4b0599a2dcc3d83d455c9be4e8a5033b7175c1859bfa634d2a3367553e0a.png)\n\nFinally, to get the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x),$ we take all the points that belong to ${T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}$ or ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}:$\n\n![](images/46/4683bc52b9d18e7710b593d36ca191adeee6ecbc93428e1f40dd7161794090d8.png)"}]}
